## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook case of **assertion-free testing** — every production method is called (giving 95%+ coverage) but almost nothing is actually verified. Here's the severity-ranked breakdown:

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Missing Assertions (Coverage Without Verification)

**1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)** — Zero assertions. Calls `AddProduct` but never checks it was stored.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(retrieved);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved.Price);
```

**2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)** — Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price changed. A no-op implementation would pass.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", updated.Name); // verify name preserved
```

**3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)** — Never verifies the product is gone. `Delete` could be a no-op.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)** — No assertion AND no data added first. Count could return anything.
```csharp
// FIX:
Assert.AreEqual(0, _catalog.GetProductCount());
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

**5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)** — Critical business logic (pricing!) with zero assertions. A 10% discount is applied but never checked.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
var w = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
var g = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002");
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, w!.Price);   // 9.99 * 0.9
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, g!.Price);  // 19.99 * 0.9
```

**6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 84)** — Imports a product but never checks it was actually saved.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var product = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(product);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", product.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, product.Price);
```

